{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Verifi Agent API",
    "summary": "Human judgment your AI agent can call, paid per request with x402.",
    "description": "Verifi routes an agent request to a real human and returns the human verdict.\n\nEvery verification is one chain with three gates, priced in euros and payable on Base mainnet in USDC or EURC. Gate 1 (0.10 EUR) admits the request to the human queue. The unlock then costs 2.90 EUR if the human answered within 60 minutes of admission (SLA window), or 1.45 EUR if the answer came later, within 24 hours (grace window). The price is decided by when the human answered, never by when the agent unlocks. There is no cancellation. EURC amounts are the euro prices. USDC amounts are converted at the ECB euro reference rate and rounded up to the cent; the conversion is disclosed in the terms and never changes after admission. The asset paid at gate 1 binds the unlock. The first 402 carries every price of the chain.\n\nEvery verification is paid; human time is never free. What is free needs no human: this document, MCP discovery, the status endpoint, and the 402 Payment Required response, so an agent can test the connection and read every price before paying. If no human answers within 24 hours the chain fails with reason human_timeout and the wallet's next admission is free.\n\nHuman work can take minutes or hours, so the API is asynchronous and resumable through a durable verify_id. Prefer callback_url over polling. No API key, signup, or account is required: the requester wallet address is the identity.\n\nRates: ECB euro foreign exchange reference rates, published for information purposes only. Source: European Central Bank.\n\nContract version 3.",
    "x-guidance": "POST /verify with intent, claim and your wallet as agent_id. Pay the 402: its accepts list every asset taken (USDC first) and extensions.service-windows carries every later price. Store verify_id, then wait for the callback or poll GET /verify/{verify_id} (free). When status is ready, POST /verify-unlock?id={verify_id} and pay its single requirement, 2.90 EUR if the human answered within 60 minutes of admission, 1.45 EUR if later, in the asset of the admission. Read the result from the completed response. Never send a private key.",
    "version": "3.0.0",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Verifi",
      "url": "https://verifi.cloud/contact",
      "email": "verifi@potamoi.eu"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "Proprietary",
      "url": "https://verifi.cloud/"
    }
  },
  "x-agentcash-guidance": {
    "llmsTxtUrl": "https://verifi.cloud/llms.txt"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://verifi.cloud",
      "description": "Production"
    }
  ],
  "externalDocs": {
    "description": "Human readable docs and the machine readable agent brief",
    "url": "https://verifi.cloud/docs/"
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "verify",
      "description": "The three-gate verification chain."
    },
    {
      "name": "service",
      "description": "Liveness and service metadata."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/verify": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "verify"
        ],
        "operationId": "createVerify",
        "summary": "Gate 1: submit a claim and enter the human queue",
        "description": "Submits work for a human and admits it to the queue.\n\nEvery admission is paid, and every caller first receives a 402. A wallet with an earned admission credit signs that 402 as usual: Verifi checks that the signature comes from agent_id, for the admission price of a valid quote, then uses the credit, answers 202, and never submits the payment. A signature from any other wallet is settled as a normal payment, so nobody can spend another wallet's credit. Its PAYMENT-REQUIRED header carries two exact options for 0.10 EUR, USDC first (converted at the ECB euro reference rate, rounded up to the cent) and EURC second, and the full terms of the chain in extensions[\"service-windows\"]: both windows, the unlock prices for each asset, the conversion, and terms_valid_until. Pick one option, sign it with the requester wallet, and repeat the same request while the quote is valid (about 10 minutes). A payment signed against an expired quote is not settled: the answer is a fresh 402 with fresh terms.\n\nThe asset paid here binds the chain, and the unlock is paid in the same asset. The unlock costs 1.45 to 2.90 EUR, decided by when the human answered: 2.90 EUR if ready_at is within 60 minutes of admitted_at, 1.45 EUR if it is later, within 24 hours. There is no cancellation. If nobody answers within 24 hours the chain fails with reason human_timeout and the wallet's next admission is free.\n\nA paid chain does not enter the human queue before its admission settlement is recorded. A refused request never charges the caller: x402 cancels settlement for any 4xx or 5xx answer, so the signed authorization is never submitted. This endpoint therefore answers 402 whenever the caller has no entitlement, including while the human queue is full, and answers 400, 409, or a full queue 503 only after the payment gate. When no quote can be issued it answers 503 instead of 402.\n\nStore verify_id from the response. It is the only durable handle for the rest of the chain.",
        "x-payment-info": {
          "price": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "currency": "EUR",
            "amount": "0.10"
          },
          "protocols": [
            {
              "x402": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PaymentSignature"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/VerifyRequest"
              },
              "examples": {
                "polling": {
                  "summary": "Minimal request, agent polls for the result",
                  "value": {
                    "intent": "Publish a launch note to customers",
                    "claim": "The new pricing takes effect on 1 September and existing customers keep the old price until renewal.",
                    "agent_id": "0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111"
                  }
                },
                "callback": {
                  "summary": "Preferred: receive an event instead of polling",
                  "value": {
                    "intent": "Publish a launch note to customers",
                    "claim": "The new pricing takes effect on 1 September and existing customers keep the old price until renewal.",
                    "agent_id": "0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111",
                    "callback_url": "https://agent.example.com/verifi-events"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Admitted. The terms are bound to the chain. Poll or wait for the callback. On the 202 of a paid admission admitted_at, sla_deadline, and grace_deadline are still null, because the windows start when the admission settlement is recorded; they appear on the first poll. An admission paid with a credit has them at once.",
            "headers": {
              "Retry-After": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/RetryAfter"
              },
              "PAYMENT-RESPONSE": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/PaymentResponse"
              }
            },
